  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array of numbers, find the minimum number of operations needed to make it palindromic, where in each operation you can select any two adjacent elements, add them, and replace them with their sum.\n\nNote: A palindromic array reads the same forwards and backwards.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of testcases.\nEach test case contains two lines,\n\nThe first line contains the number of elements in the array NNN.\nSecond line contains NNN space separated integers\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nOutput the minimum number of operations needed to make the array palindromic",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4\n1 2 3 4\n4\n1 4 5 1\n3\n1 1 1",
        "output": "3\n1\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1: [1, 2, 3, 4]\n\nOperation 1: Add 1,2 -> [3, 3, 4]\nOperation 2: Add 3,4 -> [3, 7]\nFinal array [3, 7] is not yet palindromic\nOperation 3: Add 3,7 -> [10]\nFinal array [10] is palindromic (single element is always palindromic)\nTotal operations = 3"
      }
    ]
  },
